      "description": "Building on the knowledge acquired in ITAL1000, this course aims to further develop students’ ability to communicate in Italian in various everyday situations. It also seeks to give students a taste of Italian culture and invites them to explore cultural differences. Through intensive practice students will develop more confidence in interacting in Italian while further expanding and solidifying their understanding of the basic grammar and pronunciation patterns.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "1. Not for students who have taken ITAL2001,2050,3000,3001,3002,3050 or 3051 \n2. Prerequisite: ITAL1000",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Classwork\nInteractive Tutorial",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "academic_org": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "learning_outcomes": "The students at the end of the course will have enforced the correct pronunciation, getting much more familiar with its different features. They will be able to lead a conversation about practical common situations, such as asking for and giving directions, talking about family members and about past events, getting and giving recommendations, etc. The same skills will be developed for the written language (reading and writing), and the course will also continue to transmit to the learners a good knowledge of the Italian culture, and a good of the country and its lifestyle.",
